Asset Licensing Policy
======================

Source code in this repository is licensed under the MIT License; see LICENSE.
This file covers everything else — art, audio, fonts, and other non-code assets,
principally under `assets/`.

Every bundled asset is either **CC0 1.0** (public domain, no attribution required)
or **CC BY 4.0** (attribution required). Per-asset provenance — source URL, author,
license, and retrieval date — is recorded in ASSETS.md.

If you ship a game built on this starter
----------------------------------------

Copy the ready-made attribution block from CREDITS.md into your credits. It is
pre-written and covers every CC BY asset here. That is the whole obligation: no
research, no per-file bookkeeping. Assets marked CC0 in ASSETS.md require nothing
at all, and you may of course replace any asset with your own.

What may never be committed here
--------------------------------

- CC BY-NC or CC BY-ND (non-commercial or no-derivatives)
- GPL / AGPL / any copyleft licence
- Marketplace EULAs (Fab, Unity Asset Store, Unreal) — these forbid redistributing
  the raw asset files, which is exactly what a public repository does
- Any licence with a no-redistribution-in-collections clause. A starter kit *is* a
  collection; "Custom CC0 with restrictions" is not CC0.
- Anything of unverified origin

On user-upload sites such as Freesound and OpenGameArt, licences are self-declared
and can be wrong. Our defence is provenance, not licence text — hence the retrieval
date in ASSETS.md.

The governing principle: a starter kit must not impose obligations on the games
built with it beyond a single pasted credits block.

